[h1]Deep Space AI: Probably DeepSeek — Pawnshop Maid Assistant "Xiaojing"[/h1]
Xiaojing is your AI maid in the pawnshop. Click her portrait to ask for help picking goods, organizing stock, or carrying out jobs that take several checks and actions.

[h2]What Xiaojing can do[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Run errands[/b]: move and sort stock, fill and pour liquids, print bottles, operate machines, and transfer finished products.
[*][b]Check the details[/b]: look up customer budgets and preferences, inspect items and durability, read notes and guides, and flag certain visitors when they arrive.
[*][b]Work the way you like[/b]: chat travels with your game save. Use F7 to set up your model, prompt, game tips, and quick replies.
[/list]

[h2]Quick replies: send a whole procedure in one click[/h2]
F7 → Quick replies lets you save five buttons. A message can include several steps, conditions, and reasons to stop. Unlock the faucet and gather supplies to try “Purify water (2 batches).” Xiaojing fits a filter into a 3,000 mL pitcher and fills it, rechecks durability, and temporarily stores the water if the filter needs replacing. She treats it with UV and two purification tablets, then checks how much the purifier's storage tank actually received from each batch. The job stops if durability is unknown or if supplies or tank space run out.

Clicking a quick reply sends the entire instruction to Xiaojing. She works out the next step from current stock and tool results, so it's handy when the job needs a fresh judgment each time.

[h2]Macros: save a routine and run it in the game[/h2]
[list]
[*]Ask Xiaojing to draft a macro. For example, “Make a water treatment macro that asks for a batch count and stops if supplies run out.” You can also edit the JSON directly in Manage macros.
[*]Review and approve the draft, then click its button in chat. If the macro takes inputs, such as a batch count, the game asks for them before running it.
[*]Macros support branches, loops, and checks, and look up items in the current save at run time. Built-in game tools run locally without model requests between steps. If a run stops, the result shows where it stopped and what was completed.
[/list]
Your local macro library is shared across saves. Use quick replies for jobs you want Xiaojing to reason through and macros for procedures you want to repeat. See the [url=https://github.com/Mooooooon/ProbablyAI/blob/main/docs/hands-api.md]tool guide[/url] for the macro format and a starter example.

[h2]📝 Changelog[/h2]
[b]v0.7.18[/b]
[list]
[*]Create, review, and run local macros from chat. Macros support conditions, loops, and inputs.
[*]Ask the assistant to draft a macro, then approve it to run it in one click. Approved macros are available across local saves.
[*]Pouring routines can check that the full amount will fit and record how much actually reached the target.
[/list]

[i]See the [url=https://github.com/Mooooooon/ProbablyAI/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md]GitHub changelog[/url] for the full release history.[/i]
[h2]🛠️ Quick Start & Notes[/h2]
[list]
[*]1. When enabling the mod in Mods menu, confirm the network permission prompt, then restart the game.
[*]2. In the pawnshop, press [b]F7[/b] to configure your API endpoint and API Key (DeepSeek API recommended; stored locally).
[*]3. Xiaojing strictly follows native game mechanics and will not spawn items or auto-complete transactions.
[/list]

